A||||2||CanadianGT||Re-Installation of ECM||||9||
Z||000000||CanadianGT||03-14-2001||05:43 PM||||In September I started to remove the engine from my 86GT, and I removed the ECM.  Shortly after I got in a car accident, badly broke my arm, and did not touch my car again for 3 months.  So just last week I started to work on my car again, and for the life of me I cant figure out where these 4 little clips go on my ECM (2 small Blue, 2 Larger Grey).  I know they have something to do with the ECM, but I cant remember how they go on, and I seem to have tried every way!! Any help as to how these go on, would be greatly appreciated!<BR>Thanks.||||reg||9
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||03-14-2001||05:53 PM||||First welcome to the forum.<P>The gray plugs should fit into a plug set on the back end of the console, they are setting on top of the plastic skeleton frame to which you bolt the arm rest/console.<P>The blue ones should plug into the ecm, just match the sizes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Jay||03-14-2001||06:42 PM||||Welcome fellow Canadian.  The plugs on the ECM can be a bit tricky to put back into place.  It can be frustrating because you know they go into that slot but they don't seem to want to fit.  Take a deep breath and line it up then push.  I would advise on getting a Hayes manual.  They are available at "Canadian Tire" for about $10-15.<P>What are you doing to the car? engine swap?||||reg||1
